    "text": "By AJ Woodson ,\n9 hours ago With the 2026 midterm elections approaching, Democrats should be preparing to capitalize on what many political analysts consider a favorable political environment. President Donald Trump’s approval ratings continue to face challenges over inflation, gas prices, and criticism surrounding his administration’s handling of the conflict with Iran. Yet instead of presenting a unified strategy, the Democratic National Committee (DNC) finds itself battling financial instability, internal conflict, and growing questions about its leadership. Read full article",
